#!/usr/bin/env python3
# apply_lot_compounding.py — fence LOT_COMP_20260924
#
# Calendar-stepped lot compounding for EVERY backtest strategy + Compare-page
# capital columns. Backtest-only: no paper/live file is touched.
#
#   Config keys (top level):  lot_comp_step_months, lot_comp_add_lots
#   Backtest page:            "Compound step (months)" + "Lots per step" in
#                             Run parameters (blank/0 = off → keys omitted)
#   Runners (17):             per-day lots for NEW entries; carried positions
#                             keep their entry lots; every leg scales by the
#                             same ratio; ₹ knobs scale with the ratio
#   Compare runs:             Margin cell "base → peak", KPI rows Capital
#                             (peak lots) + Return on peak capital, Key
#                             params "Compound +1L / 3mo · 10→34L"
#   Portfolio:                exposure uses each trade's own qty
#   SweepBuilder:             two axes (lot_comp_step / lot_comp_add)
#
# Run ONLY this script (it carries its payloads):
#   cd /Users/anbu/dev/scalp-app && python3 apply_lot_compounding.py [--allow-dirty] [--skip-tests]
#
# Safety: fence presence check (abort if applied), prerequisite fences
# asserted, `git status` stop-sign on targets (override with --allow-dirty),
# every edit applied in memory + py_compile before ANY write, staged
# all-or-nothing writes with .bak-LOT_COMP_20260924 backups, desktop tree
# mirrored when present, unit + runner suites + esbuild parse afterwards.
